{"step_index":519,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-25T12:10:21Z","input_tokens":2096,"cache_read_tokens":54102,"output_tokens":2238,"thinking":"The request involves adding interactive learning to a process, specifically prompting users to predict outcomes before certain steps. These prompts should cover variable value changes, conditional evaluation, and overall result alterations, with optional functionality.\n\n\nA toggle control is needed to enable/disable interactive \"Predict Mode,\" ensuring normal operation when deactivated. When Predict Mode is active, specific steps, like variable updates or conditional checks, must trigger interactive questions. These questions should present clear prompts and multiple-choice options, pausing the process until answered, followed by the correct result and explanation.\n\n\nIdentifying the steps needing interactive questioning requires analyzing common program operations. Compound arithmetic assignments and assignments with arithmetic operations are key candidates for predicting value changes. Conditional statements also warrant prediction prompts to assess understanding of program flow.\n\n\nFocusing on implementing the interactive elements, three main question types emerge: variable assignment prediction, conditional statement evaluation, and variable update confirmation. Each type will require a specific format: a clear question, multiple-choice options, a correct answer, and an explanatory justification. The assignment questions should consider potential errors for distractors, like off-by-one calculations. Condition tests will focus on boolean evaluation of logical expressions. Update confirmation questions will assess understanding of the impact of conditions on variable state changes.\n\n\nNow considering how to dynamically generate interactive questions based on the code's execution steps. Augment assignments and arithmetic assignments will trigger \"what will target become?\" questions. Conditional statements will prompt \"True or False?\" questions. Assignment to a result variable (like `ans`) will trigger a \"what value gets assigned?\" question. The UI should display one interactive element at a time before proceeding.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/index.html\"","EndLine":"60","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Inspecting top bar in index.html\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect top bar in index.html\""}}]}
