orrect answer will be based on whether the condition evaluates to True or False. For the condition `if c < 0:`, the question will be \"Will this condition (c < 0) trigger a reset of c to 0?\". The options will correspondingly be \"Yes, reset c to 0\" or \"No, keep c = [current value of c]\".\n\n\nFocusing on generating interactive questions for the code execution steps. Prioritizing questions for additions (`c += nums[i]`), conditional checks (`if c >= ans:`, `if c < 0:`) and assignments (`ans = c`). The goal is to promote active learning by prompting predictions on key variable changes. For additions, questions will be \"What will the variable become after this addition?\" with multiple-choice answers, including the correct value, original value, and an incorrect calculation. Conditional questions will ask \"Will this condition be True or False?\". Assignment questions will involve predictions on variable updates like \"Will ans change?\".\n\n\nAnalyzing how to control the display and interaction of the prediction quiz based on the \"Quiz Mode\" toggle. When enabled, the quiz card will appear for steps containing generated questions and not yet answered. When disabled, the quiz card will be hidden, and navigation will be direct. The visual state transitions will provide immediate feedback, marking correct and incorrect answers and revealing explanations. These answers will be stored for persistent review.\n\n\nIf Quiz Mode is active during Auto Play, the execution will pause at unanswered prediction questions, displaying a toast notification. The \"Next Step\" button will function even with a pending question, either revealing the answer or advancing smoothly with a \"Skip & Reveal\" option on the question card. Question data will be generated within the explanation enrichment process, attaching a `quizQuestion` object to each step. Example question data will include a unique ID, question type, the question itself, contextual hints, and multiple-choice answer options.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"view_file","args":{"AbsolutePath":"\"C:/Users/CVT/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/code-flow-visualizer/app_build/engine.js\"","EndLine":"60","StartLine":"1","toolAction":"\"Inspecting engine.js start\"","toolSummary":"\"Inspect engine.js presets\""}}]}
